# Reference list of the environment variables pirate-radio reads. Nothing loads
# a `.env` file automatically: export these in your shell profile, or put them
# in your agent's MCP server config `env` block (see docs/sources.md).

# --- Spotify (optional; only needed for /spotify-* commands) ----------------
# 1. Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
# 2. Under "Redirect URIs" add EXACTLY: http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
# 3. Copy the Client ID here.
# The redirect URL isn't actually reached — pirate-radio uses PKCE and asks you
# to paste the `code` query param back with /spotify-complete-login.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# --- HÖR Berlin (optional; YouTube bot-check auth for yt-dlp) ---------------
# Set ONE of these. A cookies.txt export always works; a browser name works
# while Firefox is open, but Chrome/Edge must be fully closed on Windows.
HOER_COOKIES_FILE=
HOER_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=

# --- Session scope (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Give each concurrently running MCP session a distinct value, and use the same
# value for that session's CLI commands.
PIRATE_RADIO_SESSION=
